# Check that BOLT can process bzip with Arm SPE profile and the resulting binary
# works correctly.
# This example uses a pre-generated SPE profile in textual format which
# was created by Linux Perf script command.
#
# Why does this example rely on a textual format SPE profile?
# - To collect an Arm Spe profile by Linux Perf,
#   it needs to have an arm developer device which has Spe support.
# - To decode SPE data, it also needs to have the proper version of Linux Perf.
#   The minimum required version of Linux Perf is v6.15.
#
# The textual format profile was created by the following steps:
# 1)
#  - Gather SPE profile by using Perf
#     $ perf record -e 'arm_spe_0/branch_filter=1/u' -- ./bzip2 bzip2.copy
# 2)
#  - Generate a textual format profile by using Linux Perf script command:
#     $ perf script --show-mmap-events -F pid,brstack --itrace=bl  -i perf.data
REQUIRES: native,system-linux,target=aarch64{{.*}}

# Convert the profile
RUN: perf2bolt %p/Inputs/bzip2 -p %p/Inputs/perf.text -o %t.fdata -perfscript --spe --ignore-build-id \
RUN:   |& FileCheck %s -check-prefix=CHECK-P2B

# Optimize using that profile
# Check that llvm-bolt processes bzip2 binary for aarch64 in these conditions:
#   - block reordering
#   - function splitting
#   - no relocs
RUN: llvm-bolt %p/Inputs/bzip2 -o %t  -dyno-stats \
RUN:   -data %t.fdata -reorder-blocks=cache -split-functions \
RUN:   |& FileCheck %s -check-prefix=CHECK-BOLT

# Check the resulting binary
RUN: %t %p/Inputs/bzip2.fdata

CHECK-P2B: PERF2BOLT: parsing a hybrid perf-script events...
CHECK-P2B: PERF2BOLT: parsing perf-script mmap events output
CHECK-P2B: PERF2BOLT: parse SPE branch events in brstack-format

CHECK-BOLT-NOT: BOLT-INFO: 0 out of {{.*}} functions in the binary (0.0%) have non-empty execution profile
